Legal AI Harness — NOTICE
=========================

NOT LEGAL ADVICE
----------------
This software assists with legal workflows. It does not practice law, it is
not a lawyer, and its output is not legal advice. Every output must be
reviewed by qualified counsel before being relied on for advice, filings,
negotiations, or operations. The citation-verification stack reduces — but
does not eliminate — the risk of fabricated or unsupported authority.

Primary sources
---------------
The harness retrieves statutes, regulations, and judgments from third-party
and government databases (PKULaw, 国家法律法规数据库, eCFR, Federal Register,
GovInfo, CourtListener, EUR-Lex, EASA, CAAC, ECAA, and others). Those sources
carry their own terms of use, rate limits, and licensing. Using a connector
means accepting the terms of the source it calls; check them before
redistributing retrieved text.

Corpus binaries
---------------
No corpus documents are distributed with this repository. The RAG corpus
manifests under legal_helper/rag/corpus/*/manifest.yaml describe documents
that are fetched on demand from their publishers. ICAO documents, CAAC
attachments, and treaty texts remain the copyright of their respective
publishers.

